{"classification":"mathematical-measure-domain-mismatch","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0239","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The product measure lives on R^r x R^r while h lives on R^r; the conclusion integrates h against the convolution measure nu, so its domain and null sets are the required structures.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt257.tex:51-53","source_text":"domain $\\Lambda$ of product measure $\\lambda$ used to qualify $h$ on $\\BbbR^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt257.tex:51-53","target_text":"domain $\\Sigma$ of convolution measure $\\nu$ used for measurability and almost-everywhere qualification","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S257"}
{"classification":"mathematical-false-probability-normalization","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0240","math_ordinal":89,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The measures are only totally finite, not probability measures; the convolution density integrates to the product of their total masses, which is finite but need not equal one.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt257.tex:117","source_normalized_sha256":"bdf78b93a8718813e880be7c900f41d81e1cc1d2c8b85917f3b6521dcc327603","source_text":"$\\int f_1*f_2d\\mu=1$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt257.tex:117","target_normalized_sha256":"4519ad78e25a53064d423595979628e77827044bf8415a76a8864867c6caffb2","target_text":"$\\int f_1*f_2d\\mu=\\nu_1(\\BbbR^r)\\nu_2(\\BbbR^r)<\\infty$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S257"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-measure","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0241","math_ordinal":94,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"No unindexed nu is bound in 257F; the theorem and preceding calculation concern the convolution nu_1*nu_2.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt257.tex:131","source_normalized_sha256":"84eb2b123d1102b8f7c00b34116df32107cffa82d46efbac7fd9543fa7459c38","source_text":"Radon-Nikod\\'ym derivative of $\\nu$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt257.tex:132","target_normalized_sha256":"e8af9f75a8a8ecd41d68b8f4e6dbddb0126efa244c71f97eb792fbb6e9ee8fcd","target_text":"turunan Radon--Nikod\\'ym dari $\\nu_1*\\nu_2$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S257"}
{"classification":"mathematical-unbound-quantified-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0242","math_ordinal":104,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The identity uses nu but the source noun phrase omits the measure name; inserting nu binds the quantified symbol without changing the claim.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt257.tex:141","source_text":"for every totally finite Radon measure on $\\BbbR^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt257.tex:141-142","target_normalized_sha256":"84eb2b123d1102b8f7c00b34116df32107cffa82d46efbac7fd9543fa7459c38","target_text":"untuk setiap $\\nu$ yang merupakan ukuran Radon berhingga total pada $\\BbbR^r$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S257"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-space","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0243","math_ordinal":167,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Exercise 257Ya defines M over Borel subsets of the real line and binds no r; its L1 subalgebra must use Lebesgue measure on the same real line.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt257.tex:192","source_normalized_sha256":"6a5173578402ab704fe0e78c24a3f6f09fe9ed2c7ea0fbe574d688249eb91ed7","source_text":"Lebesgue measure on $\\BbbR^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt257.tex:193","target_normalized_sha256":"22316cdc991b42844c0fcdb72f227b6d4c0e8457a736e325af2845b7b3df7f6c","target_text":"ukuran Lebesgue pada $\\Bbb R$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S257"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-measure","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0244","math_ordinal":173,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH25-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The circle-model definition introduces nu and never defines mu; Sigma is the domain of the measure nu whose completeness and approximation properties are being specified.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt257.tex:199-200","source_normalized_sha256":"492247e1bab15272d1e53b8015c042bf6fa0cb8f23ec52cad93d6ba80dafb804","source_text":"domain $\\Sigma$ of $\\mu$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt257.tex:200-201","target_normalized_sha256":"84eb2b123d1102b8f7c00b34116df32107cffa82d46efbac7fd9543fa7459c38","target_text":"domain $\\Sigma$ dari $\\nu$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S257"}
